        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_792121f873d84f56b691b1527bdfa73d",
      "statement": "env_vars::validate() checks every typed production variable before the runtime starts so cached or synchronous-callback readers become infallible without defaults; variables are classed as flags (CELLD_OUTPUT_GATE, CELLD_LTX_COMPACTION, CELLD_UNSAFE_PUBLIC_ADVERTISE, CELLD_TRUST_FORWARDED_HEADERS, ...), required-positive integers (CELLD_ACTIVATIONS, CELLD_RELEASES, CELLD_SHUTDOWN_*, CELD_TTL_MS among others), optional integers (CELLD_MAX_RESIDENT_CELLS, CELD_MAX_RSS_MB, CELD_READY_FLEET_GATE_MS, CELD_DRAIN_TOKEN_WAIT_MS), and enumerated (CELLD_LOG_TRANSPORT must be http or stream).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/env_vars.rs#L15-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0c822e54c714396ce35eb64825546025c3385e9117eb8be543e462b3d35320c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_78792f491c7540329d196d0870cc0d05",
      "statement": "Range-constrained variables exist too: CELD_PRESENCE_HEARTBEAT_MS must be between 50 and 30000, and CELD_V8_HEAP_LIMIT_MB must be a representable positive megabyte count.",
      "evidence": [
