    {
      "id": "claim_7819e09639304db982d822960721c485",
      "statement": "Documented variable interactions: a CELD_MAX_RSS_MB at or above 95% makes the 95% cgroup cap the effective limit (reported at startup) and 0 disables both the threshold and the cap; during a rolling restart, operations should wait for restoring=0 on every node before restarting the next (diagnose reports `restoring=`); the per-isolate V8 heap limit CELLQD_V8_HEAP_LIMIT_MB (default 128 MB) is separate from node memory, governs WS client capacity, and an isolate re-serves after falling under 75% of the limit.",
